I am back in the flat.
I go into the kitchen.
I set the bags on the counter.
Now I unpack everything.
I sort my purchases.
I put the cheese straight into the fridge.
Rice, pasta and coffee go into the cupboard.
The shelves are finally full again.
The cupboards are not empty anymore.
I put the tomatoes and the apples into a bowl.
The bowl stands on the table.
I take the bread and the bread roll out of the bag.
I want to eat the bread roll right away.
But there is still the kohlrabi.
I do not know the kohlrabi.
But I like new vegetables.
It does not go into the fridge.
The kohlrabi stays on the counter.
Tomorrow I want to cook the kohlrabi.
